# Redis Rate Limiting Verification Commands
# You can execute these commands in redis-cli to check Spring Cloud Gateway rate limiting states.
# Connection command: docker exec -it chat_redis redis-cli

# 1. List keys associated with rate limiting (typically configured under request_rate_limiter namespace)
KEYS *request_rate_limiter*

# 2. Check the token count of a sliding window rate-limiter bucket (Replace placeholders)
# KEYS:
#  - request_rate_limiter.{userId}.tokens (Remaining tokens in bucket)
#  - request_rate_limiter.{userId}.timestamp (Last replenishment timestamp)

# 3. Retrieve the remaining token count (Replenished based on configure rate limits)
# GET request_rate_limiter.UUID.tokens

# 4. View TTL on rate-limit counter keys (should match the rate window, e.g. 1 minute)
# TTL request_rate_limiter.UUID.tokens
